5. Create distance feature
data["distance"] = np.sqrt(    (data["dropoff_longitude"] - data["pickup_longitude"])**2 +    (data["dropoff_latitude"] - data["pickup_latitude"])**2)



Explanation:
- data["distance"] – Creates a new column called distance.
- dropoff_longitude – Longitude of the drop-off location.
- pickup_longitude – Longitude of the pickup location.
- dropoff_latitude – Latitude of the drop-off location.
- pickup_latitude – Latitude of the pickup location.
- **2 – Calculates the square of a value.
- np.sqrt() – Calculates the square root.
This uses the Euclidean distance formula:
\[
d=\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2}
\]

Purpose: To calculate the approximate distance between pickup and drop-off coordinates.
print("\nAfter Pre-processing:")print(data.head())



