What is R² score?
R² stands for Coefficient of Determination.

It measures how well the model explains the variation in the target variable.
- R² closer to 1 = Better fit.
- R² around 0 = Model explains little variation.
- R² below 0 = Model performs worse than a simple mean-based prediction on the test data.
What is RMSE?
RMSE stands for Root Mean Squared Error.

It measures the average size of prediction errors, giving more weight to larger errors.
- Lower RMSE = Better prediction accuracy.
- Higher RMSE = Larger prediction errors.
Remember: Higher R² and lower RMSE generally indicate a better model.
