Important practical corrections
Your code is suitable for understanding and demonstrating the three regression models. However, remember these points:
1. Distance calculation: Your formula calculates straight-line distance in latitude-longitude coordinate units, not actual kilometers. For real travel distance, Haversine distance is more appropriate.
2. Data leakage: Ideally, calculate outlier limits using only training data after splitting, rather than using the full dataset before splitting.
3. Standardization: Ridge and Lasso generally work better when input features are standardized. Your current code does not standardize them.
4. Model tuning: Ridge() and Lasso() use default regularization strengths. Their performance can change when you tune alpha.
